# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or use install script).
#
# --- No paid domain? Use nip.io (free) ---
# If your public IP is 54.252.233.98, use hostname:
#   54.252.233.98.nip.io
# (nip.io DNS resolves that name to that IP; Caddy + Let's Encrypt work.)
# Install: sudo PUBLIC_IP=54.252.233.98 bash deploy/https/install-caddy-nip.sh
#
# --- Or use your own domain ---
# DNS A record: YOUR_DOMAIN -> EC2 public IP
# Security group: TCP 80, 443 (and 22 for SSH)
#
# API must listen on 127.0.0.1:8000 (docker-compose.ec2.yml).
#
# Twilio webhook:
#   https://<hostname>/api/v1/webhooks/twilio/messages
#
# After editing: sudo systemctl reload caddy

YOUR_DOMAIN {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
